A||||8||Adrift||Body Filler Cracks?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||09-07-2001||11:05 AM||||I've been using body filler to fix up small (1/4 inch at largest) dents and holes. Someone recently told me to lay fibreglass instead of using bodyfiller, because body filler will just crack off in the future? Is this something I should be worried about, or more of an urban legend?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||09-07-2001||12:42 PM||||I think fiberglass is better .But I am not abody repair man.I have seen bad body repairs done with bondo maybe it was not mixed right not sure but I think fiberglass is stronger ||||reg||1
Z||000002||jch82||09-07-2001||01:08 PM||||It depends on where you use the bondo. I have never used fiberglass but from fixing cracks and what not on my 85GT, there are definitely spots to use bondo and other times it isnt appropriate...<P>If the spot where the crack is tends to flex or move a lot, chances are that the bondo is going to crack again in the future. Bondo isn't very forgiving when it comes to flexing. For spots that are somewhat flexible, I use flexible parts repair from 3M. It is a two-part epoxy and has worked excellent on my front nose. I had a crack about 4 inches long right down the center and since I used that stuff (its been about 2-3months) it hasnt cracked yet! Anyone that lives in MI knows how $hitty the roads are....Hope this helps<P><BR>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82(sig).jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||09-07-2001||02:22 PM||||Its for a crack around the turn signal area (the space which the turn signal sits in), so will I be ok with body filler?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||09-07-2001||02:50 PM||||If your talking about on the front, use the flexible bumper repair kit.<BR>If your talking about on the rear above or beside the lense, use bondo or fiber fill. If your meaning the rear bumper, flexible kit.<P>Hope this helps you out!<BR>IRG||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||09-07-2001||06:02 PM||||use flexible repair filler for bumper, reg body filler for anything else. Broken or cracked in 2 needs glass. I have a body shop by the way. Body filler is usually as flexible as orig panel. The idea of cracking off was in the old days when it d ried rock hard. you have to grind or sand all paint off where you put it though.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroFanaticus2||09-07-2001||06:35 PM||||I've been using something called bondo-glass for repairs to my hood and also for glassing in a hood scoop.<BR>It's kind of like fiberglass, but a little easier to work with I think.  I just mix it up goop it on with a putty knife then sand it down once it gets hard.  I then run a thin layer of bondo body filler over it just to fill in little pin holes, then I sand it down so it's even again.  Works really well for me. <P>But for regular flexible body panels I would use flexible bumper repair stuff.  I have a crack in a rear bumper that fierodave gave me when I bought the hood and scoop from him that I will be fixing in the next week or so using a bumper repair kit.  Instructions are on the box and it seems pretty simple, but FieroDave warned me that it'll smell like dog ****  really bad, so be ventilated.<P>I've never done any body work before I started on the hood scoop, but I am amazed at how simple it really is.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||09-08-2001||12:05 AM||||bondo glass is nothing like fiberglass. It is bondo with chop in it to give it some strength.<BR>I also use bondo resin when it is approiate.||||reg||1
Z||000008||jch82||09-08-2001||02:23 AM||||I was told to use something called 'vette adhesive for the hood scoop I am getting. It is wind tested at like 110mph and comes in gallon cans. It is available at almost any store that sells paint supplies (or so i was told).....<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82(sig).jpg"> ||||reg||5
